Distributed supply chains reduce transportation distances, environmental impacts, and supply chain vulnerabilities while enabling more responsive, localized production systems. By moving manufacturing closer to markets, companies can reduce logistics emissions, improve delivery times, and create opportunities for modular, on-demand production that better matches consumer needs. This approach supports the reuse and circular economy by enabling local repair, refurbishment, and remanufacturing networks. Distributed networks also facilitate knowledge sharing and innovation across geographies while maintaining quality control and brand consistency.